  "conclusions": [
    "Full DR reduces mean forward velocity RMSE under randomized evaluation by 46.02810431405205% versus baseline, with improvement in all three training seeds.",
    "Full DR reduces randomized mean RMSE by 10.171643618354395% versus fixed-delay DR; seeds 42 and 43 improve while seed 44 is essentially tied.",
    "Full DR increases nominal mean RMSE by 28.568632539976164% versus baseline; the robustness result has a nominal-condition tradeoff.",
    "No fall-reduction claim is supported because every method had zero observed falls.",
    "No overall smoothness-improvement claim is supported: applied-target rate and acceleration increase in all three seeds, and actual joint acceleration changes have mixed signs.",
    "The strongest supported finding is improved forward-tracking robustness within the evaluated dynamics range."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only three independent training seeds per method; 2304 episodes are not 2304 independent training replicates.",
    "Baseline versus full DR compares a package that includes broader initialization and changed mean actuator dynamics.",
    "Full DR versus fixed-delay DR compares joint variation of lag and delay at matched parameter centers; it does not separately identify lag and delay effects.",
    "Evaluation uses held-out seeds within training parameter ranges, not out-of-distribution dynamics.",
    "This is a local reference simulation study; it is not the official course score and does not establish hardware performance.",
    "The seed-42 baseline and full-DR training runs were reused as declared; development evaluation seed 2042 was excluded from this study's formal evaluation.",
